Yes, this is the GTK front-end. gtkhack needs to connect to a server
which runs the actual game while gtkhack deals with the GUI part.
While it's possible to connect to servers on other machines via a
network, you can also simply connect to a local server by specifying
the location of an executable. The RPM should be configured with the
location of the Slash'EM binary as the default server (named local)
so just selecting this from the list and clicking on the "connect"
button should start the connection. Once gtkhack has finished
downloading the tileset etc., that it needs it will display the main
window and wait for input. You can then change any options you want
before starting a game by using the "Play" menu.

Appologies for the lack of a man page for gtkhack.

